{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456265-v5-more-realistic-embraces-and-the-nights-to-follow","id":1456265,"title":"[V5] More Realistic Embraces, and the Nights to Follow","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-06T14:43:31-07:00","id":1456265,"title":"[V5] More Realistic Embraces, and the Nights to Follow","content":"The embrace is a dramatic time for all involved. The mortal has undergone a powerful transformation, often feeling agony and rage, and the sire may feel a mix of emotions depending on the situation entirely. However, I haven\u2019t seen many Storytellers represent this process or the nights after in the dramatic weight it deserves. So after some quick research, here are a few rules for portraying the embrace and following nights in the 5th edition of VTM.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">The Newly Embraced</span></b><br /> The newly created undead are inexperienced, very much drained, and likely on the verge of frenzy. New born kindred start out with no Disciplines, Clan Weakness, or Predator Type. They start with the Generation minimum for the Blood Potency, and almost always start at Hunger 5, unless their sire feeds them more then a single drop.<br /> <br /> Once feed even a single drop of vitae, the newborn immediately wakes up. If the newly embraced is a Thin-Blood, however, it can take them several hours before they awaken. Once awake, the new kindred needs to make a Hunger Frenzy check, unless their sire feeds them enough to lower their hunger to at least Hunger 3. Welcome to the undead life.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Storytellers Rolls</span></b><br /> When a kindred awakens after the embrace, roll 4 10-sided dice, and record them from lowest to highest, reroll 1s. These tell you when the newborn will develop their kindred traits. The first number tells you how many nights it takes for the vampire to develop their Clan Weakness, and the next 3 tell you when they develop their in-clan disciplines, gaining 1 dot each night. For example, if the lowest was a 3 then they'll develop their Clan Weakness on the 3rd night.<br /> <br /> These changes can be sudden or gradual, depending on the story\u2019s tone and pacing. Some Clan Weaknesses, such as the Nosferatu\u2019s, develop over the nights leading up to the last night when the Clan Weakness fully settles. How the Storyteller represents this gradual change is up to the Storyteller.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Health and Bodley Changes</span></b><br /> Draining someone dry is painful and 100% leaves some severe damage to the newly embraced. Most new-bloods start with at most 5 points of aggravated damage. If this damage would fill the new-blood\u2019s healthy tracker completely, replace the last point with superficial damage instead. While they have this damage, the new-blood experiences a burning sensation which is the body removing all waste and living matter.<br /> <br /> As they heal, many physical deformities may or may not develop or worsen as the kindred adjusts to their new form. The opposite is also true, as once hideous individuals may slowly become more and more beautiful as the embrace fully settles. In game terms, a player can elect to rework merit advantages and associated flaws. They must always have the same number of dots as when they started, and any removed flaws will be replaced with flaws of similar value.<br /> In addition, the body may heal itself to a point of use, such as the lame being able to walk and the blind suddenly being to see. This is 100% a case-by-case basis and is completely up to the Storyteller if it should happen.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Predator Type</span></b><br /> It can take several months, or even years, for the newly embraced to develop a Predator type. Ultimately, it is up to the Storyteller when a vampire will develop, but a good rule of thumb is that a vampire needs to hunt as their intended predator type multiple times before choosing it. Even Thin-Bloods can develop a Predator Type, but most don't live long enough to do so.<br /> <br /> For more variable Predator Types, see my post <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454106-v5-custom-predator-types\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Thin-Bloods and Caitiffs</b></span><br /> Caitiffs and Thin-Bloods are an unusual lot. A Storyteller can elect to have a newly embraced kindred become a Caitiff whenever they please, but it is more common in abandoned childer. When rolling in the Storyteller Roll section, drop the first dice and use the last three.<br /> <br /> For Thin-Bloods, this is much more tricky. Ask the player, or yourself, how many Thin-Blood Merits they want, minimum 1 or a maximum of 3. Roll that number of dice, and record the results from lowest to highest. The Thin-Blood develops those Merits, and Flaws, on those nights after the embrace. For Example, if you roll a 5 as the lowest, they\u2019ll develop their first Thin-Blood Merit and Flaw in the 5th night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":26764,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","user":"Vilenecromancer","date":". 08-06-2021, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-07T02:03:16-07:00","id":1456289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456265-v5-more-realistic-embraces-and-the-nights-to-follow#post1456265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> TWhen a kindred awakens after the embrace, roll 4 10-sided dice, and record them from lowest to highest, reroll 1s. These tell you when the newborn will develop their kindred traits. The first number tells you how many nights it takes for the vampire to develop their Clan Weakness, and the next 3 tell you when they develop their in-clan disciplines, gaining 1 dot each night. For example, if the lowest was a 3 then they'll develop their Clan Weakness on the 3rd night.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes a great deal of sense for this to be a gradual process following the Embrace. It is nice to see clear mechanics given for this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456265-v5-more-realistic-embraces-and-the-nights-to-follow#post1456265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The opposite is also true, as once hideous individuals may slowly become more and more beautiful as the embrace fully settles. In game terms, a player can elect to rework merit advantages and associated flaws. They must always have the same number of dots as when they started, and any removed flaws will be replaced with flaws of similar value.<br /> In addition, the body may heal itself to a point of use, such as the lame being able to walk and the blind suddenly being to see. This is 100% a case-by-case basis and is completely up to the Storyteller if it should happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that you included this part. It fits with Vampirism being a superior state of being. And what predator would be burdened by physical imperfections? The way I imagine it, Toreador Vampires especially become distinctly more beautiful (more so than other Vampires, though some would argue with this...), while Gangrel Vampires might become slightly more physically imposing, for example.<br /> In regard to removing disabilities of the body - this is clearly shown in the <i>Lasombra Revised Clanbook</i> introductory short story, where the viewpoint character notes while being Embraced that he can feel his legs again, after years of being paralyzed from the waist down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 08-09-2021, 06:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-07T05:02:35-07:00","id":1456296,"title":"","content":"Interesting. Strengely I was working on something along these lines just this morning.<br /> Disciplines<i> are</i> a matter of nurture over nature, I believe. I think the Setite Warrior bloodline develops through training a fledgling from embrace to make them one, causing them to develop potence instead of obfuscate. Without that training they're just regular members of their clan. By extension, while that fledgling is inclined to develop Protean/Serpentis, Presence and Obfuscate, one can theorise that if they were ditched somewhere with no guidance they would have a chance to develop disciplines more appropriate to their experiences instead (and become Caitiff).<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure there's text to suggest clan weakness sets in at embrace, though.<br /> The Nosferatu's body starts breaking and rebuilding itself into an abomination from the moment of embrace and lasts days to weeks, as I recall, leaving them helpless and in agony beyond imagination. The Hecata write up flat out states that they experience the Underworld and Oblivion between death and waking up, and it's an experience unique to their clan and that's what defines them as the Clan of Death. I'd also expect them to wake up screaming bloody murder, assuming they can with their neck torn out. And I think it was mentioned somewhere that Malkavians like to stick around when a new fledgling wakes up, usually in groups, because the clan curse hits immediately and often like a truck. The fledgling needs to be taken out of the public eye until they're stable or &quot;stable&quot;, may need to be restrained, and some of them are judged too dangerously unstable to let live. Can't remember where I saw that, but I'm sure I did. Maybe the clanbooks, but I haven't looked at them for years, so I might double check.<br /> <br /> I'd also throw in a rule that the newly embraced, lacking any experience with their clan weakness, hunger or the beast, are at a severe penalty to control themselves that only goes away with practice. Like you've got a permanent penalty to resist frenzy that only goes down bit-by-bit as you actually experience frenzy and learn to recognise one coming on and dial it back, or something like that. Still working on the specifics, but a newborn fledgling can be dangerous and unstable.<br /> (Of course, how well they learn, and how quick, is likely to depend on their environment and sire. A well fed fledgeling in a stable environment who gets introduced gradually and carefully to their new instincts in going to have a smoother transition into unlife than, say the subject of a typical gangrel embrace who gets turned and dumped on the roadside then left to their own devices for a month.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 08-07-2021, 08:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-07T19:25:32-07:00","id":1456328,"title":"","content":"Cool idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456265-v5-more-realistic-embraces-and-the-nights-to-follow#post1456265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They start with the Generation minimum for the Blood Potency, and almost always start at Hunger 5, unless their sire feeds them more then a single drop.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have them start at Hunger 10. The sire has drained all of the blood already in their body. They need to give a lot of it back for the childe not to be hungry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Draining someone dry is painful and 100% leaves some severe damage to the newly embraced. Most new-bloods start with at most 5 points of aggravated damage. </div> </div> </div>I don't think is always necessary. If the sire roughs them up, or if the childe is Embraced while already dying, sure. But the simple act of draining a mortal's blood and replacing it with vampire blood comes out to a net change of zero.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As they heal, many physical deformities may or may not develop or worsen as the kindred adjusts to their new form. The opposite is also true, as once hideous individuals may slowly become more and more beautiful as the embrace fully settles. In game terms, a player can elect to rework merit advantages and associated flaws. They must always have the same number of dots as when they started, and any removed flaws will be replaced with flaws of similar value.<br /> In addition, the body may heal itself to a point of use, such as the lame being able to walk and the blind suddenly being to see. This is 100% a case-by-case basis and is completely up to the Storyteller if it should happen. </div> </div> </div>This is pretty in-keeping with the game's lore. Chicago by Night 1e had a member of the Wolf Pack get in a motorcycle accident and lose the use of his legs. After his Embrace, he hopped back onto the motorcycle.<br /> <br /> Pretty sure Lestat's dying and tuberculosis-riddled (or was it some other disease?) mom in The Vampire Chronicles also gets sexied up when Lestat Embraces her.<br /> <br /> I don't see that happening with every Embrace, though. Not all vampires are supermodels and there are plenty who had Appearance 2 in V20 and older editions.<br /> <br /> I think these changes would be most pronounced in low-generation childer, especially ones who are 7th or below. It's as the curse of Caine weakens, and there's increasingly little difference between mortals and vampires, that being &quot;upgraded&quot; to a vampire carries fewer perks. I like the idea that thin-bloods are basically unchanged from their mortal selves and the Embrace may not even fix problems it's normally guaranteed to, like cancer or AIDS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-08T02:19:46-07:00","id":1456338,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it was always a fluff thing that the Embrace rounds out imperfections, improves Perception and makes you more graceful and powerful. They never gave it mechanics but I always assumed the extra Attribute and Ability dots went some way towards reflecting this. E.g. add +1 dot to Appearance and +1 dot to Perception, as well as extra dots in Awareness, Alertness, Athletics, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-08T12:13:25-07:00","id":1456363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456265-v5-more-realistic-embraces-and-the-nights-to-follow?p=1456338#post1456338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it was always a fluff thing that the Embrace rounds out imperfections, improves Perception and makes you more graceful and powerful. They never gave it mechanics but I always assumed the extra Attribute and Ability dots went some way towards reflecting this. E.g. add +1 dot to Appearance and +1 dot to Perception, as well as extra dots in Awareness, Alertness, Athletics, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see it simply being the rationale for PCs holding the traits that they do. 7/5/3 starting Attributes creates a pretty exceptional person. One explanation is that some of it comes from the Embrace.<br /> <br /> Requiem, whose mechanics I so love to reference, gives PCs +1 Attribute dot upon Embrace. I could also see a low-generation enough Embrace handing out a bigger bonus, like an extra dot for every generation below 8th.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T03:23:54-07:00","id":1456401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456265-v5-more-realistic-embraces-and-the-nights-to-follow?p=1456296#post1456296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I think it was mentioned somewhere that Malkavians like to stick around when a new fledgling wakes up, usually in groups, because the clan curse hits immediately and often like a truck. The fledgling needs to be taken out of the public eye until they're stable or &quot;stable&quot;, may need to be restrained, and some of them are judged too dangerously unstable to let live. Can't remember where I saw that, but I'm sure I did. Maybe the clanbooks, but I haven't looked at them for years, so I might double check.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is in the<i> Revised Malkavian Clanbook</i>. Though the impression I got is that the tradition of maintaining a vigil during the Embracing of new Malkavians has also a lot to do with a strong sense of community, and caring for each other, that the Malkavians have as a Clan. (Though what Clan does not have a strong sense of community, now to think of it? They all do, in various ways. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456265-v5-more-realistic-embraces-and-the-nights-to-follow?p=1456363#post1456363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Requiem, whose mechanics I so love to reference, gives PCs +1 Attribute dot upon Embrace. I could also see a low-generation enough Embrace handing out a bigger bonus, like an extra dot for every generation below 8th.</div> </div> </div> </div>Newly Embraced Vampires of the 4th and 5th Generations, considering they are young/future Methuselahs, could gain even greater bonuses. Say, the elevation of one group of Attributes to 5s or 6s, innate advancement in multiple Disciplines, some nice Merits (without getting any Flaws), etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 08-09-2021, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}